* ===========================================================================
* ERSATZ_PATH_LADDER_REDIRECT_PROOF.DTS
* Runtime proof for AIF-145 R-a steps 1-3b: ERSATZ now resolves workspace,
* .erz and .dot targets through ladder 2 (dottalk::paths) instead of its own
* private copy.
*
* Status:  PROOF / READ-ONLY
* Safety:  NON-MUTATING. Every command below is either a report or a LOAD of
*          a name chosen BECAUSE IT DOES NOT EXIST. Nothing is written, no
*          table is opened, no workspace is saved.
* Lane:    AIF-145 (path ladder divergence)
* Commits: 3f6428921 step 1, b01ca5127 step 2, 65ddfe806 step 3a,
*          97854db87 step 3b
*
* HOW TO RUN
*   $env:X64BASE_ALLOW_DATA = "1"
*   .\datarun.ps1
*   Standalone:  DOTSCRIPT scripts/ersatz_path_ladder_redirect_proof.dts
*   Capture:     SET ALTERNATE TO <file> / SET ALTERNATE ON  (never
*                DOTSCRIPT OUT -- AIF-081, still unfixed)
*
* STOP_ON_ERROR IS OFF BELOW, AND THAT IS A HAZARD WORTH NAMING.
* Every block here is SUPPOSED to fail: each one LOADs a name chosen because
* it does not exist, and the failure text is the measurement. With
* STOP_ON_ERROR ON the run would abort at B2. With it OFF, a run in which
* NOTHING resolved would still finish looking calm -- this lane has already
* had one fixture fail green. So the pass condition is NOT "the script ran".
* It is: six blocks printed, and each printed path matches its prediction.
* A missing block is a failure even though the run stayed green.
*
* WHY THE TARGETS DO NOT EXIST
* The redirect is only OBSERVABLE on the not-found path. When a file exists,
* both ladders return the same absolute path -- that is the whole claim, and
* a passing "same file" tells you nothing about which ladder answered. The
* INVENTED path is where the two ladders were always allowed to differ, so
* that is where the proof has to look.
*
* ERSATZ prints the resolved path inside its failure text ("cannot open
* file: <path>", "expected .erz file, not script file <path>"), so the
* resolver's answer is visible without any new instrumentation.
*
* ===========================================================================
* PREDICTIONS -- WRITTEN BEFORE THE RUN. Do not edit after running.
* ===========================================================================
*
* Let USERWS = the USER WORK line printed by ERSATZ STATUS
*     DATA   = the data root (parent of DATA WORK)
*
* B1  ERSATZ STATUS
*     Prints ten root lines. USER WORK must end in \user\default\workspaces.
*     This report still runs on LADDER 3 -- it was deliberately NOT switched
*     in 3b. It agrees with ladder 2 today only because current_profile_name()
*     returns the literal "default" and s.current_user defaults to "default".
*     This line is the control: if it ever stops matching B2, identity has
*     been wired and the report is the thing left behind.
*
* B2  ERSATZ LOAD zzz_no_such_profile
*     BARE NAME, does not exist. Ladder 2 falls back to roots.front(), which
*     IS the current-user workspaces root, so this must be UNCHANGED by the
*     redirect.
*     PREDICT: cannot open file: <USERWS>\zzz_no_such_profile.erz
*
* B3  ERSATZ LOAD zzz_sub/zzz_no_such_profile
*     THE ONE CHANGED CASE. Separator-bearing and non-existent. Ladder 3
*     invented <USERWS>\zzz_sub\...; ladder 2 invents under the DATA root.
*     PREDICT: cannot open file: <DATA>\zzz_sub\zzz_no_such_profile.erz
*     A <USERWS> answer here means the redirect did NOT take effect.
*
* B4  ERSATZ LOAD zzz_no_such_script.dot
*     Reaches the .DOT guard, which resolves through the SCRIPT roots and
*     rejects. Bare name, so roots.front() = current-user SCRIPTS root.
*     PREDICT: expected .erz file, not script file
*              <USER SCRIPT>\zzz_no_such_script.dot
*
* B5  ERSATZ LOAD zzz_sub/zzz_no_such_script.dot
*     Same changed case, script side.
*     PREDICT: expected .erz file, not script file
*              <DATA>\zzz_sub\zzz_no_such_script.dot
*
* B6  ERSATZ WLOAD zzz_no_such_workspace
*     Reaches resolve_workspace_target, redirected in step 2 (b01ca5127).
*     Bare name, extension search .dtschema then .dtschemas, neither exists,
*     so the conventional location under the PRIMARY extension is named.
*     PREDICT: a path ending \zzz_no_such_workspace.dtschema -- NOT
*              .dtschemas, and NOT a bare name with no extension.
*
* ===========================================================================
* AMENDMENT 2026-08-28, AFTER STEP 3c (b30f27aad)
*
* B1's prediction above says the report "still runs on LADDER 3 -- it was
* deliberately NOT switched in 3b." That was true when written and is now
* FALSE: step 3c moved print_session_status onto ladder 2 and then deleted
* ladder 3 outright. The prediction is left VERBATIM because this block is
* dated evidence, not documentation -- rewriting a prediction after the fact
* is how a fixture stops being a fixture. The B1 echo line in the body was
* corrected, so a fresh run's B1 header differs by that one string from the
* transcript recorded below.
*
* B1 still measures something, and arguably something better: it is now the
* control proving 3c did NOT move any value. Third run 2026-08-28 against
* build b30f27aa -- all ten root lines byte-identical to the two runs before
* it, while their SOURCE changed from ladder 3 to ladder 2. A report whose
* output is unchanged and whose authority moved is exactly what an inert
* consolidation should look like.
*
* The day B1 and B2 disagree is the day identity was wired (AIF-144) -- and
* now that both read ladder 2, they will follow the acting user together
* instead of drifting apart. That was the point of 3c.
* ===========================================================================
* RUNTIME STATUS: GREEN 2026-08-28, 6/6 blocks, every path as predicted.
* Ran against build "v0.6 (2026-08-27, 97854db8 dirty)" -- the banner hash is
* commit 97854db87, step 3b itself, so the binary under test contained the
* redirect. ("dirty" was this file, untracked at run time. The Aug 27 stamp is
* local time; the commit is 02:xx UTC Aug 28.)
*
*   B1  USER WORK  = ...\dottalkpp\user\default\workspaces
*   B2  ...\user\default\workspaces\zzz_no_such_profile.erz      UNCHANGED
*   B3  ...\data\zzz_sub\zzz_no_such_profile.erz                  CHANGED
*   B4  ...\user\default\scripts\zzz_no_such_script.dot          UNCHANGED
*   B5  ...\data\zzz_sub\zzz_no_such_script.dot                   CHANGED
*   B6  ...\zzz_no_such_workspace.dtschema  (primary ext, not .dtschemas)
*
* B3 is the load-bearing one. It is the ONLY input the redirect changes, and
* it answered under the DATA root. B2 is its control and did not move. Both
* had to hold: a run where B3 moved and B2 moved too would mean the fallback
* changed wholesale, not that ERSATZ started using ladder 2.
*
* WHAT B1 ALSO SHOWED, WHICH WAS NOT PREDICTED
* USER WORK and DEFAULT WORK print the SAME directory
* (user\default\workspaces), and so do USER SCRIPT and DEFAULT SCRIPT. The
* search-root list is written as four roots {current-user, public, default,
* data} but holds THREE distinct directories today, because the current user
* IS "default". Any test that believes it is distinguishing a current-user
* rung from a default rung is not distinguishing anything yet -- the two
* become distinct only when identity is wired (AIF-144). Recorded here so
* that a future green on a "user beats default" assertion is not mistaken
* for evidence.
* ===========================================================================

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

? "=========================================================="
? "AIF-145 R-a REDIRECT PROOF -- ladder 2 resolves ERSATZ paths"
? "=========================================================="

? " "
? "--- B1: ERSATZ STATUS (roots report -- ladder 2 since 3c) ---"
ERSATZ STATUS

? " "
? "--- B2: bare name, not found -- must be the USER workspaces root ---"
ERSATZ LOAD zzz_no_such_profile

? " "
? "--- B3: separator + not found -- THE CHANGED CASE, expect DATA root ---"
ERSATZ LOAD zzz_sub/zzz_no_such_profile

? " "
? "--- B4: bare .dot -- script roots, expect USER scripts root ---"
ERSATZ LOAD zzz_no_such_script.dot

? " "
? "--- B5: separator + .dot -- changed case, script side ---"
ERSATZ LOAD zzz_sub/zzz_no_such_script.dot

? " "
? "--- B6: WLOAD bare name -- expect .dtschema, not .dtschemas ---"
ERSATZ WLOAD zzz_no_such_workspace

? " "
? "=========================================================="
? "PROOF RUN COMPLETE -- compare each block against its"
? "prediction in the header of this script."
? "=========================================================="
